From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] egl/dri2: do not strdup() a NULL device_name when binding a wayland display

dri2_bind_wayland_display_wl() asks drmGetRenderDeviceNameFromFd() for the
render device name and, when there is none, falls back to
strdup(dri2_dpy->device_name) without checking that device_name is set.

With the GBM backend on its software fallback there is no render device:
fd_render_gpu is only opened when the device is not a software one, and
device_name is filled in from that fd. A display controller without a GPU
node gets there as soon as the hardware driver cannot create a screen (GBM
then falls back to kms_swrast/swrast). Binding a Wayland display on such an
EGL display, which the Qt Wayland compositor does at start-up through its
wayland-egl hardware integration, then ends in strdup(NULL):

  Program terminated with signal SIGSEGV, Segmentation fault.
  #0  strlen ()
  #1  strdup (s=0x0)
  #2  ?? () from /usr/lib/libEGL.so.1

seen with Mesa 26.0.5 on an LG Nexus 5 running a mainline kernel whose msm
DRM device has no GPU (surface-manager of LuneOS, started with
-platform eglfs).

The caller already handles a NULL device_name: the next line takes the fail
path and eglBindWaylandDisplayWL() returns EGL_FALSE, which is what a
compositor expects when the display cannot be shared. So only the strdup()
needs guarding.

Tested on that device: with the stock libEGL surface-manager dies with the
backtrace above under every Qt Wayland hardware integration (wayland-egl and
both linux-dmabuf variants); with this patch it starts and keeps running.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
@@ -2695,7 +2695,7 @@
       goto fail;
 
    device_name = drmGetRenderDeviceNameFromFd(dri2_dpy->fd_render_gpu);
-   if (!device_name)
+   if (!device_name && dri2_dpy->device_name)
       device_name = strdup(dri2_dpy->device_name);
    if (!device_name)
       goto fail;
